THEOREM 4: PAIR AUTOMATON SPEEDUP
The pair automaton enables O(m)-time DP for aggregate computations
while naive iteration requires O(F_{m+2}) = O(phi^m) time.
======================================================================

n=5: Pair DP sum(H_approx)=246, brute=153, ✓: False
       Pair DP count=34, F_{m+2}=21, ✓: False
       True sum(H)=159 (vs approx 153)
       Average H_approx=7.286, average H_true=7.571

The Pair DP computes sum(H_approx) in O(m) time:
  vs naive O(F_{m+2}) = O(phi^m) time

